---
import { Heading, Markdown } from '@splendidlabz/astro'
import { FancyList } from '@splendidlabz/astro/svelte'
---

<section class="section bg-zpurple-900">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="vertical">
      <Heading class="gap-4 mb-2" center>
        <h2 class="h1 text-zorange-500 max-w-[16em]">
          <Markdown>
            How much better will your HTML and CSS be 30 days later?
          </Markdown>
        </h2>
      </Heading>

      <div class="prose-responsive max-w-[37rem] mx-auto">
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <Markdown>
          Will you:
        </Markdown>
      </div>

      <div
        class="grid-simple bp9:[--cols:2] max-w-[60rem] mx-auto gap-4 items-center"
      >
        <div class="vertical gap-2">
          <p class="text-center italic text-neutral-400">
            <Markdown inline
              >Keep doing the same thing you've been doing:</Markdown
            >
          </p>
          <div
            class="prose card p-3 rounded-1r"
            style="border-color: var(--color-zred-500); background-color: var(--color-zred-850);"
          >
            <FancyList
              class="ml-0 simple-svg fill-zred-500 text-zred-50"
              icon="ph:x"
              items={[
                'Write pure Tailwind or pure CSS',
                'Create layouts from scratch over and over again',
                'Struggle with using more than 2 typefaces',
                'Wire up themes by scattering colour variables everywhere',
                'Copy-pasting complex effects from online sources',
              ]}
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="vertical gap-2 italic text-neutral-400">
          <p class="text-center">
            <Markdown inline>... or try something entirely new</Markdown>
          </p>
          <div
            class="prose card border-scaffold p-3 rounded-1r"
            style="border-color: var(--color-zgreen-500); background-color: var(--color-zgreen-900);"
          >
            <FancyList
              class="ml-0 simple-svg text-zgreen-50 fill-zgreen-500"
              icon="ph:check"
              items={[
                'Use Tailwind and CSS together',
                'Build layouts using a quick and proven system',
                'Use multiple typefaces easily',
                'Theme easily with pigments and variables',
                'Get effects like nice shadows by dropping a utility',
              ]}
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-responsive max-w-[37rem] mx-auto">
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <Markdown>
          The choice is yours.

          You already know you have a growing sense of dissatisfaction every time you open your HTML or CSS file.

          **The real hidden cost is ignoring that dissatisfaction** --- knowing you can be doing better than this, yet doing nothing about it.

          30 days later, things can be very different from where they are today. You can be happy and satisfied with how your HTML and CSS look.
        </Markdown>

        <a
          href="#pricing"
          class="button button-large pigment-orange-filled self-center"
        >
          <Markdown inline>Get Unorthodox Tailwind</Markdown>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
